  "question": {
    "text": "A metal <math> <mrow> <mtext>(P)</mtext></mrow> </math> on heating in nitrogen gas gives compound <math> <mrow> <mtext>Q</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow> </math> <math> <mtext>Q</mtext> </math> on treatment with <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> gives a colourless gas which when passed through <math><mtext>CuS</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> solution gives a dark blue-violet coloured solution. <math> <mtext>P</mtext> </math> and <math> <mtext>Q</mtext> </math> respectively, are",
